{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>See, HaShem has called by name Betzalel.</b> Moses said: See and examine precisely their names, for HaShem called by name Betzalel — for from the very start HaShem gave them names that indicate they were created for this, that they would be engaged in the work of the Sanctuary. For Betzalel is on account of צֵל אֵל (the shadow of El), an allusion that he would build the Mishkan and the Ark, in which is the dwelling of the Shekhinah that comes under the shadow of its beams, as it is written (Psalms 91:1) ״יוֹשֵׁב בְּסֵתֶר עֶלְיוֹן בְּצֵל שַׁדַּי יִתְלוֹנָן״, and it is written (Song of Songs 1:13) ״בֵּין שָׁדַי יָלִין״ — our Rabbis of blessed memory explained this regarding the Holy One, blessed be He, who would contract His Shekhinah between the two staves of the Ark and between the two cherubim that cover the face of the kapporet with their wings, and סְכָךְ (covering) means צֵל (shadow), for they were צֵל אֵל, the shadow of El, as it were. And the proof is that in all the work of the Mishkan it is written ״וַיַּעַשׂ״ without mentioning Betzalel, but regarding the Ark it is written ״וַיַּעַשׂ בְּצַלְאֵל אֶת הָאָרוֹן״. All of this is proof that he is called בְּצֵל אֵל on account of the Ark. בֶּן אוּרִי — on account of אוֹר הַתּוֹרָה (the light of Torah), for he would build a place for the Torah, which is light. בֶּן חוּר — הוֹרָה שֶׁבַּדִּין (the instruction of justice) — it was fitting to bring him near to this holy work more than others, because Hur, his grandfather, surrendered his life over the making of the calf that caused the breaking of the tablets, for according to our Rabbis of blessed memory (Sanhedrin 7a) they killed Hur. לְמַטֵּה יְהוּדָה — which is compared to a lion's whelp, and the Sanctuary is called Ariel. Just as this lion is broad in front and narrow behind, so the Mishkan was broad in front and narrow behind, to teach that the place of the Shekhinah does not depend on the spreading out of hands, for the heavens and the heavens of the heavens cannot contain Him, yet this House does. Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, chose for His Shekhinah a narrow place, to teach that He is not confined by any place, and for the honor of Israel He overrode His own honor to be contained in a place. In any event He chose for Himself a narrow place, and this remark suffices for the discerning." "<b>He and Oholiav.</b> He was so named because he would build the Ohel Mo'ed (Tent of Meeting) for our Father in heaven, and on this account he was called by the name Oholiav. ״בֶּן אֲחִיסָמָךְ״ — for that is the name of the place of the leaning (סְמִיכוּת) of the brothers, that is, the Shekhinah with Israel, as it is written (Psalms 122:8) ״לְמַעַן אַחַי וְרֵעָי אֲדַבְּרָה נָּא שָׁלוֹם בָּךְ״, and it is written (Song of Songs 2:2) ״אֲחֹתִי רַעְיָתִי״. ״לְמַטֵּה דָן״ — which is also compared to a lion's whelp, as it is said (Deuteronomy 33:22) ״דָּן גּוּר אַרְיֵה״; therefore it is fitting that he should build the Ariel. And He alluded through Yehudah and Dan to two of His names, blessed be He — יהוה אלהים, the Name of mercy and the Name of justice — with which the Holy One, blessed be He, partnered and created the world. So too this Mishkan, which was made on the pattern of all the worlds, was made through Yehudah, in whose name the entire Name of mercy is included, and through Dan, which indicates the attribute of justice. For with these two HaShem formed His world, and with these two the Mishkan — fashioned on the pattern of the world — was made, through the tribe of Dan and Yehudah. Therefore it is said <b>See, HaShem has called by name</b>, and this secret is sound and clear.\n\nAnd in order that the building of the Mishkan resemble in every way the building of the world, Moses commanded to proclaim ״אִישׁ וְאִשָּׁה אַל יַעֲשׂוּ עוֹד מְלָאכָה״ — and all this, why? Did they commit a transgression by bringing more than necessary? Rather, because Moses saw that the design of this building is a replica of the building of the world in its entirety, and our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Chagigah 12a): when the Holy One, blessed be He, created the world, it kept expanding further and further, until the Holy One, blessed be He, rebuked it and said to His world: דַּי (enough). So too, when Moses saw that this matter was going and expanding without end, he rebuked them, saying ״אַל יַעֲשׂוּ עוֹד מְלָאכָה״, for thus did the Holy One, blessed be He, do in the creation of His world.\n\nAnd regarding what is written ״וַיִּקְחוּ מִלִּפְנֵי מֹשֶׁה״, some say that Moses, out of concern for suspicion, did not want to bring the donation into his house and chambers; rather, when it was set down before him, from there the craftsmen took it."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "The phrase לְהוֹרוֹת שֶׁמְּקוֹם הַשְּׁכִינָה is straightforward; no ambiguity."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:25:48.990243127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}